Build frontend with Vite + React + router. Need node installed (yes). Create frontend folder at project root.

Plan:
- npm create vite@latest frontend -- --template react (non-interactive). Then npm install react-router-dom axios.
- Structure:
  frontend/src/api/client.js
  frontend/src/auth/AuthContext.jsx
  frontend/src/auth/ProtectedRoute.jsx
  frontend/src/components/... (e.g., FormField? Loading? ErrorMessage?)
  frontend/src/pages/LoginPage.jsx, RegisterPage.jsx, HomePage.jsx (protected placeholder dashboard)
  frontend/src/styles/*.css (styles separate): index.css, auth.css, layout.css
  App.jsx with routes
  main.jsx with BrowserRouter

Auth approach: token storage. Simple: access & refresh in localStorage (spec's simple approach; not httpOnly cookies). Store user object too, but refresh on load via /me to validate.

client.js: axios instance baseURL from VITE_API_URL default http://127.0.0.1:8000/api. Request interceptor adds access. Response interceptor: on 401 and not refresh request, single-flight refresh with queue, retry original; on failure clear tokens and redirect to /login (dispatch event or window.location). Avoid duplicate refresh calls: module-level refreshPromise.

Avoid circular import with AuthContext: client exports token helpers (getTokens/setTokens/clearTokens) and `onAuthFailure` callback registration; AuthContext registers handler.

AuthContext:
- state user, initializing
- on mount: if access token exists тЖТ GET /auth/me/ тЖТ setUser; catch тЖТ try refresh handled by interceptor; if fails clear.
- login(email,password) тЖТ POST /auth/login/ тЖТ store tokens+user
- register(payload) тЖТ POST /auth/register/ then auto-login? Requirement registration works; simplest: register then login automatically. That's nice. Or redirect to login with success message. Auto-login after register is smoother; but register response has no tokens. So call login after successful registration. Do that.
- logout() тЖТ POST /auth/logout/ with refresh (needs access), then clear local state regardless of response.

Login form: email, password, loading, error. Show field errors from API (non_field_errors/detail).

Register form: email, full_name, phone, password, password2 client check. Server errors mapping.

ProtectedRoute: if initializing show loader; if !user тЖТ Navigate to /login state={{from}}; else children/Outlet. Also maybe role-based? Task only auth. Keep simple `ProtectedRoute` with Outlet.

Pages: HomePage (protected) simple "╨Ы╨╕╤З╨╜╤Л╨╣ ╨║╨░╨▒╨╕╨╜╨╡╤В" with user info + logout button + note catalog soon. Not catalog.

Routing:
