content.text:
Interesting: navigating to `/catalog` no longer redirects to login because the previous run left the session in localStorage (the user-data-dir persists). The e2e expects a clean session. So before starting, clear storage: `Storage.clearDataForOrigin` or evaluate localStorage.clear() then reload. Better: at start, after connecting target, enable, navigate to APP origin, clear localStorage, then navigate /catalog.

Implement: 
```
await send("Page.enable");
await send("Runtime.enable");
await navigate(`${APP}/login`);
await evalJs("localStorage.clear()");
await navigate(`${APP}/catalog`);
```
But wait: navigate to /login while session exists тЖТ PublicOnlyRoute redirects to /catalog, but then we clear storage and navigate again. That's fine, but we should wait readyState. Simpler: navigate to `${APP}/login`, then localStorage.clear(), then navigate(`${APP}/catalog`) and expect /login redirect.

However, careful: `navigate` waits for root children; after PublicOnlyRoute redirect to /catalog it renders. Then clear.

Alternative: use CDP `Storage.clearDataForOrigin` with origin `http://localhost:5173`, storageTypes "local_storage". Cleanest: send("Storage.clearDataForOrigin", {origin: APP, storageTypes: "local_storage"}). Need Storage domain maybe just call. Then navigate.

I'll do: after enabling Page/Runtime, `await send("Storage.clearDataForOrigin", { origin: APP, storageTypes: "local_storage" });` тАФ should work without enabling.

Then navigate /catalog тЖТ expect /login.

Also note during the failed run, the previous run left tokens; session persisted. Add also check that after logout tokens are cleared (already).

Let me patch script.

input.newString:
await send("Page.enable");
await send("Runtime.enable");

// 1. Catalog requires login; login lands in catalog.
// ╨Я╤А╨╛╤И╨╗╤Л╨╣ ╨┐╤А╨╛╨│╨╛╨╜ ╨╝╨╛╨│ ╨╛╤Б╤В╨░╨▓╨╕╤В╤М ╤Б╨╡╤Б╤Б╨╕╤О ╨▓ ╨┐╤А╨╛╤Д╨╕╨╗╨╡ ╨▒╤А╨░╤Г╨╖╨╡╤А╨░.
await send("Storage.clearDataForOrigin", {
  origin: APP,
  storageTypes: "local_storage",
});
await navigate(`${APP}/catalog`);

